+# Redrob: Korean, and the two things Pretendard does not carry.
+#
+# The bundled UI face covers all 11,172 precomposed Hangul syllables, so ordinary Korean needs no fallback at all
+# and renders in the brand face. It carries ZERO of the conjoining Jamo block (U+1100-11FF) and ZERO CJK Han, both
+# measured rather than assumed -- so Hanja in a document, and NFD Hangul, which is the form macOS puts in
+# filenames, had nothing to fall back to. On a minimal install that is tofu boxes in a Korean product.
+#
+# Noto Sans CJK KR covers 256/256 of the Jamo block and 20,976/20,992 Han, which is why this is the fix rather
+# than replacing Pretendard: swapping the company's global typeface to reach a block that only appears in
+# decomposed strings would cost the brand everywhere to solve it in one place.
+#
+# It is a large dependency, around 60 MB. That is the price of a Korean product that does not show boxes.
+fonts-noto-cjk
+
